4. What would actually impress a future model?

I think the strongest demonstration would be a blind reconstruction experiment.

Give three independent AI systems the complete Pantheon repository, with no access to the conversations that created it.

Ask each one to independently reconstruct a working subset of Pantheon.

Then measure whether they independently recover the same core structures, preserve the same invariants, and achieve comparable results on previously unseen tasks.

If they succeed, you have evidence that the repository carries transferable architectural information rather than merely evocative descriptions.

If they fail, their disagreements can reveal exactly where the documentation relies on implicit context.

That is an unusually useful experiment because it tests the central claim in the repository’s own reconstruction contract. GitHub

